      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "24e8644b-e22b-54e3-a2bc-11cc5b4ef3ab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Walter Horten, Reimar Horten, Horten brothers\n- Products: Horten H.IX, Ho 229, Gotha Go 229\n- Companies: Gothaer Waggonfabrik\n- Concepts: RLM designation, mass production\n- Events: late World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Walter Horten was born on 13 November 1913.\n- Reimar Horten was born on 12 March 1915.\n- Walter Horten and Reimar Horten were German aircraft pilots and enthusiasts who were sometimes credited as the Horten Brothers.\n- The Horten H.IX had the RLM designation Ho 229.\n- The Horten H.IX was also called the Gotha Go 229 when referring to the extensive redesign work by Gotha to prepare the aircraft for mass production.\n- Reimar and Walter Horten initially designed the Horten H.IX as a German prototype fighter-bomber.\n- Gothaer Waggonfabrik was intended to build the Horten H.IX late in World War II.\n- Reimar Horten died on 14 March 1994 in Villa General Belgrano, Argentina.\n- Walter Horten died on 9 December 1998 in Baden-Baden, Germany.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5b8e5eba-96ee-5636-aed7-db07d8cf4a92",
        "text": "Page: Horten Ho 229. Sentence: The Horten H.IX, RLM designation Ho 229 (or Gotha Go 229 for extensive re-design work done by Gotha to prepare the aircraft for mass production) was a German prototype fighter/bomber initially designed by Reimar and Walter Horten to be built by Gothaer Waggonfabrik late in World War II.\nPage: Horten brothers. Sentence: Walter Horten (born 13 November 1913; died 9 December 1998 in Baden-Baden, Germany) and Reimar Horten (born 12 March 1915; died 14 March 1994 in Villa General Belgrano, Argentina), sometimes credited as the Horten Brothers, were German aircraft pilots and enthusiasts.",
